ssue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.3.stable.nixpkgs [77dcf97d8]\n\n### System information\n\nnixos\n\n### Issue description\n\nVariables of static function will raise SHADOWED_VARIABLE warnings when they do not actually shadow anything.\n\nThis is really annoying because I am creating a project that is supposed to be used by another client. I cannot simply just disable the shadow-warning as they maybe need to ship it themselves, I cannot just ship a project that throws a bunch of warnings everytime you run it, but I have to use consistent naming and cannot use 3 different names for the same thing just because variable shadowing would occur in for instance a static function where it is a non-issue.\n\nNote that I cannot use `@warning_ignore(\"shadowed_variable\")` due to: #100878\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create  a script and attach it to a scene somewhere:\n\n```\nclass_name my_class extends Object\n\nvar my_var\nvar my_other_var\n\nststic func(my_var):\n    pass\n```\n\n2. Run that project\n\nOBSERVED:\nYou now get a compiler warning telling you \"my_var\" is being shadowed on line 6 when it actually is not because it lies behind a static keyword.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nn/a","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShi